# Cursor Rules — Berkah POS

- Read root `AGENTS.md` Sections 1–8 and follow its mandatory reading order before any change.
- Target stack per root `AGENTS.md` Section 3 and `docs/permanent/DOC_14_KVM2_ISOLATED_TENANT_ARCHITECTURE.md`: Laravel 13.x, PHP 8.4, Filament 5.x, Composer-locked/tested `stancl/tenancy` v3.10.x, MariaDB 11.4 LTS, Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, hosted `ubuntu-24.04` CI runners.
- The inspected Laravel migration-branch baseline is Laravel 11/PHP 8.3/Filament 3 and has no `composer.lock`; the proposal in `audit/ADR-2026-10-15-STACK-BASELINE-EXCEPTION.md` is **not approved** and does not replace Section 3 until reviewed.
- Logical config contract: `GLOBAL → TEMPLATE → TENANT → SERVICE → DEVICE`; preserve exactly 352 canonical workbook entries and the canonical keyset hash. Resolve only one requested service (`pos` or `akuntansi`).
- Keep SQLite checkout and outbox writes atomic. Do not claim cloud sync until authenticated Laravel acceptance, idempotency, durable acknowledgement, retry and conflict behavior are tested.
- Active cloud configuration uses the authenticated Laravel Central API. Historical Supabase SQL/migrations in `docs/archive/supabase-historical/` are source archives only; never apply or wire them into CI/deploy/runtime.
- Keep `btp-admin/` retired/static. The target Central Admin is authenticated Filament at `/central/admin` after deployment verification.
- Never commit credentials, URLs/tokens, production data, signing keys or hard-coded secrets. Do not expose MariaDB/Redis or provisioning credentials to the normal web process.
- Use branches and reviewed PRs only; never push implementation commits directly to `main`.
- Report source inspection, test execution, CI, staging and production evidence separately. Missing evidence is `NOT RUN / NOT VERIFIED`; do not infer acceptance from source presence.
